pcbcraft-render-server

The editing UI of PCBCraft (https://github.com/tangency-labs/pcbcraft) drawn offscreen, with no window.

The host loop (the headless graphics device, the egui pass, the offscreen paint, the read-back and the PNG
encoder) is ported from SolidZ's render server, which is itself part of the SolidCraft family
(https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft), MIT OR Apache-2.0. `adapters/painter.rs`, `adapters/readback.rs`,
`domain/damage.rs`, `domain/geometry.rs` and `build.rs` are used as they are there, with a few comments changed.

Licences: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE of the upstream tree it is built in). The editor links
SolidCraft's UI kit, look and theme through the upstream app; the licences of the third-party crates built in are in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt of a packaged build.
